{"type":"new","contents":"/-\nCopyright (c) 2025 Oliver Butterley. All rights reserved.\nReleased under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.\nAuthors: Oliver Butterley, Yoh Tanimoto\n-/\n\n\n\nimport Mathlib\nimport Mathlib.MeasureTheory.VectorMeasure.Basic\nimport Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Group.Basic\n\n/-!\n# Integral with respect to a complex-valued measure\n\nThree options come to mind for defining the integral with respect to a complex-valued measure:\n\n1. Define the integral with respect to a complex measure by decomposing the measure into real and imaginary parts and then using the definition of integral with respect to a signed measure. I.e.,\n```\nnoncomputable def integral (μ : SignedMeasure α) (f : α → G) : G :=\n    ∫ a, f a ∂μ.toJordanDecomposition.posPart - ∫ a, f a ∂μ.toJordanDecomposition.negPart\n```\nIn turn, the integral with respect to as signed measure is defined using the Jordan decomposition\ninto positive and negative parts.\n\n2. Develop directly the integral with respect to any `VectorMeasure` by introducing simple\nfunctions, etc.\n\n3. Use the polar decomposition of a complex measure into total variation measure and angular\nfunction and hence use the definition of a Bochner integral.\n\nIt is unclear what the best design choice is so at the moment we opt for using polar decomposition\nas the definition.\n\nWhatever the direction taken with these definitions, the different components should be separated\ninto their own files.\n\n## Main definitions\n\n* `ComplexMeasure.integral`\n\n## Notation\n\n* `∫ a, f a ∂μ` : integral of `f` with respect to a `ComplexMeasure` `μ`\n\n## To do\n\n* Add many other relevant results.\n\n-/\n\n@[expose] public section\n\nnamespace MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure\n\nopen MeasureTheory\n\nvariable {α : Type*} [MeasurableSpace α]\nvariable {G : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup G] [NormedSpace ℂ G]\n\n/-! ## Polar decomposition of complex measures. -/\n\nlemma variation_neg_complex (μ : ComplexMeasure α) : (-μ).variation = μ.variation := by\n  unfold VectorMeasure.variation\n  simp\n\n/-- The variation measure part in the polar decomposition of a complex measure. -/\nnoncomputable def var (μ : ComplexMeasure α) := μ.variation\n\n@[simp]\nlemma var_neg (μ : ComplexMeasure α) : (-μ).var = μ.var := by\n  simp [var, variation_neg_complex]\n\n/-- The angular part (density function) in the polar decomposition of a complex measure. -/\nnoncomputable def ang (μ : ComplexMeasure α) := μ.rnDeriv μ.var\n\n@[simp]\nlemma ang_neg (μ : ComplexMeasure α) : (-μ).ang = -μ.ang := by\n  -- To do: adjust this statement to the `μ`-a.e. version.\n  sorry\n\n/-! ## Definition of the integral. -/\n\n/-- Change of variables for the integral with respect to a complex measure defined by a density. -/\nlemma integral_withDensityᵥ_eq (μ : Measure α) [SigmaFinite μ] (h : α → ℂ)\n    (hf : Integrable h μ) (f : α → ℂ) :\n    (μ.withDensityᵥ h).integral f = MeasureTheory.integral μ (fun x => h x • f x) := by\n  dsimp [integral]\n  -- We need to show that (μ.withDensityᵥ h).var and (μ.withDensityᵥ h).ang\n  -- are related to |h| and h/|h|.\n  sorry\n\ntheorem exists_l1_eq_withDensity_variation (μ : ComplexMeasure α) :\n    ∃ h : α → ℂ, Integrable h μ.variation ∧\n    μ = μ.variation.withDensityᵥ h := by\n  let μ_re := MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.re μ\n  let μ_im := MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.im μ\n  have h_re : μ_re ≪ᵥ μ.variation.toENNRealVectorMeasure := by\n    apply VectorMeasure.AbsolutelyContinuous.mk\n    intro s hmeas hs\n    rw [Measure.toENNRealVectorMeasure_apply_measurable hmeas] at hs\n    have h_le : ‖μ s‖ₑ ≤ μ.variation s := by\n      rw [VectorMeasure.variation, VectorMeasure.ennrealToMeasure_apply hmeas]\n      exact MeasureTheory.preVariation.sum_le (‖μ ·‖ₑ) hmeas (Finpartition.top hmeas)\n    have : μ s = 0 := by\n      have : ‖μ s‖ₑ = 0 := by exact le_antisymm (hs ▸ h_le) (by positivity)\n      exact enorm_eq_zero.mp this\n    rw [MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.re_apply, this, Complex.zero_re]\n  have h_im : μ_im ≪ᵥ μ.variation.toENNRealVectorMeasure := by\n    apply VectorMeasure.AbsolutelyContinuous.mk\n    intro s hmeas hs\n    rw [Measure.toENNRealVectorMeasure_apply_measurable hmeas] at hs\n    have h_le : ‖μ s‖ₑ ≤ μ.variation s := by\n      rw [VectorMeasure.variation, VectorMeasure.ennrealToMeasure_apply hmeas]\n      exact MeasureTheory.preVariation.sum_le (‖μ ·‖ₑ) hmeas (Finpartition.top hmeas)\n    have : μ s = 0 := by\n      have : ‖μ s‖ₑ = 0 := by exact le_antisymm (hs ▸ h_le) (by positivity)\n      exact enorm_eq_zero.mp this\n    rw [MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.im_apply, this, Complex.zero_im]\n  let f_re := μ_re.rnDeriv μ.variation\n  have hf_re_int := integrable_rnDeriv μ_re μ.variation\n  have hf_re_eq := μ_re.withDensityᵥ_rnDeriv_eq μ.variation h_re\n  let f_im := μ_im.rnDeriv μ.variation\n  have hf_im_int := integrable_rnDeriv μ_im μ.variation\n  have hf_im_eq := μ_im.withDensityᵥ_rnDeriv_eq μ.variation h_im\n  let h (x : α) : ℂ := Complex.mk (f_re x) (f_im x)\n  have hf_re_c : Integrable (fun x => (f_re x : ℂ)) μ.variation := \n    Complex.ofReal_clm.integrable_comp hf_re_int\n  have hf_im_c : Integrable (fun x => (f_im x : ℂ)) μ.variation := \n    Complex.ofReal_clm.integrable_comp hf_im_int\n  have hf_int : Integrable h μ.variation := by\n    rw [show h = (fun x => (f_re x : ℂ) + (f_im x : ℂ) * Complex.I) by ext x; simp [h]; rfl]\n    exact hf_re_c.add (hf_im_c.mul_const Complex.I)\n  have h_eq : μ = μ.variation.withDensityᵥ h := by\n    ext1 s\n    intro hmeas\n    rw [VectorMeasure.withDensityᵥ_apply hf_int hmeas]\n    apply Complex.ext\n    · rw [← VectorMeasure.withDensityᵥ_apply hf_re_int hmeas, hf_re_eq, \n          MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.re_apply]\n      rfl\n    · rw [← VectorMeasure.withDensityᵥ_apply hf_im_int hmeas, hf_im_eq, \n          MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.im_apply]\n      rfl\n  exact ⟨h, hf_int, h_eq⟩\n\ntheorem exists_l1_eq_withDensity_variation_λ (μ : ComplexMeasure α) (λ : Measure α) [SigmaFinite λ]\n    (hμλ : μ ≪ᵥ λ.toENNRealVectorMeasure) :\n    ∃ h : α → ℂ, Integrable h λ ∧ μ = λ.withDensityᵥ h := by\n  let μ_re := MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.re μ\n  let μ_im := MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.im μ\n  have h_re : μ_re ≪ᵥ λ.toENNRealVectorMeasure := by\n    intro s hmeas hs\n    rw [Measure.toENNRealVectorMeasure_apply_measurable hmeas] at hs\n    have : μ s = 0 := hμλ hs\n    rw [MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.re_apply, this, Complex.zero_re]\n  have h_im : μ_im ≪ᵥ λ.toENNRealVectorMeasure := by\n    intro s hmeas hs\n    rw [Measure.toENNRealVectorMeasure_apply_measurable hmeas] at hs\n    have : μ s = 0 := hμλ hs\n    rw [MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.im_apply, this, Complex.zero_im]\n  let f_re := μ_re.rnDeriv λ\n  have hf_re_int := integrable_rnDeriv μ_re λ\n  have hf_re_eq := μ_re.withDensityᵥ_rnDeriv_eq λ h_re\n  let f_im := μ_im.rnDeriv λ\n  have hf_im_int := integrable_rnDeriv μ_im λ\n  have hf_im_eq := μ_im.withDensityᵥ_rnDeriv_eq λ h_im\n  let h (x : α) : ℂ := Complex.mk (f_re x) (f_im x)\n  have hf_int : Integrable h λ := by\n    have hf_re_c : Integrable (fun x => (f_re x : ℂ)) λ := \n      Complex.ofReal_clm.integrable_comp hf_re_int\n    have hf_im_c : Integrable (fun x => (f_im x : ℂ)) λ := \n      Complex.ofReal_clm.integrable_comp hf_im_int\n    rw [show h = (fun x => (f_re x : ℂ) + (f_im x : ℂ) * Complex.I) by ext x; simp [h]; rfl]\n    exact hf_re_c.add (hf_im_c.mul_const Complex.I)\n  have h_eq : μ = λ.withDensityᵥ h := by\n    ext1 s\n    intro hmeas\n    rw [VectorMeasure.withDensityᵥ_apply hf_int hmeas]\n    apply Complex.ext\n    · rw [← VectorMeasure.withDensityᵥ_apply hf_re_int hmeas, hf_re_eq, \n          MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.re_apply]\n      rfl\n    · rw [← VectorMeasure.withDensityᵥ_apply hf_im_int hmeas, hf_im_eq, \n          MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure.im_apply]\n      rfl\n  exact ⟨h, hf_int, h_eq⟩\n\nnotation3 \"∫ \"(...)\", \"r:60:(scoped f => f)\" ∂\"μ:70 => integral μ r\n\n/-! ## Some lemmas related to the integral. -/\n\n/-- For complex measures `μ`, `ν` and integrable function `f`: `∫ f d(μ + ν) = ∫ f dμ + ∫ f dν` -/\nlemma integral_add (μ ν : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → G) :\n    (μ + ν).integral f = μ.integral f + ν.integral f := by\n  -- Proof outline: use RN density with respect to a dominating measure λ = |μ| + |ν|.\n  sorry\n\nlemma integral_neg (μ  : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → G) :\n    (-μ).integral f = -μ.integral f := by\n  simp [integral, MeasureTheory.integral_neg]\n\nlemma integral_sub (μ₁ μ₂  : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → G) :\n    (μ₁ - μ₂).integral f = μ₁.integral f - μ₂.integral f := by\n  calc\n    _ = (μ₁ + (-μ₂)).integral f := by rfl\n    _ = μ₁.integral f + (-μ₂).integral f := by exact integral_add μ₁ (-μ₂) _\n    _ = _ := by rw [integral_neg, sub_eq_add_neg]\n\n/-- The integral is linear with respect to the measure: `∫ f d(c • μ) = c • ∫ f dμ` -/\nlemma integral_smul_measure (c : ℂ) (μ : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → G) :\n    (c • μ).integral f = c • μ.integral f := by\n  -- Proof outline: similar to `integral_add`, use RN density with respect to a dominating measure.\n  sorry\n\n/-- The integral is linear with respect to the function: `∫ (c • f) dμ = c • ∫ f dμ` -/\nlemma integral_const_smul (c : ℂ) (μ : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → G) :\n    μ.integral (fun a => c • f a) = c • μ.integral f := by\n  dsimp [integral]\n  simp_rw [smul_comm]\n  rw [MeasureTheory.integral_smul]\n\n/-- The integral is linear with respect to the function: `∫ (f + g) dμ = ∫ f dμ + ∫ g dμ` -/\nlemma integral_add_function (μ : ComplexMeasure α) (f g : α → G) :\n    μ.integral (fun a => f a + g a) = μ.integral f + μ.integral g := by\n  dsimp [integral]\n  simp_rw [smul_add]\n  rw [MeasureTheory.integral_add]\n  · sorry -- integrable check\n  · sorry -- integrable check\n\n/-- The integral of `f` against `μ` is bounded by `variation μ * ‖f‖_∞`. -/\nlemma integral_bound_of_variation_le (μ : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → G) (C : ℝ)\n    (hf : ∀ x, ‖f x‖ ≤ C) : ‖μ.integral f‖ ≤ (μ.variation Set.univ).toReal * C := by\n  dsimp [integral]\n  calc\n    ‖MeasureTheory.integral μ.var (fun x => μ.ang x • f x)‖\n        ≤ MeasureTheory.integral μ.var (fun x => ‖μ.ang x • f x‖) := norm_integral_le_integral_norm _\n    _ ≤ MeasureTheory.integral μ.var (fun _ => C) := by\n        apply MeasureTheory.integral_mono\n        · sorry -- integrable check\n        · sorry -- integrable check\n        · intro x\n          rw [norm_smul]\n          -- need ‖μ.ang x‖ ≤ 1\n          sorry\n    _ = (μ.variation Set.univ).toReal * C := by\n        rw [MeasureTheory.integral_const]\n        simp [var]\n\nend MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure\n","mtime":1778536901006}